---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Account Management">
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Account Management</h1>

    <h2>Plan Section</h2>
    <p>View and manage your subscription:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Current plan details and features</li>
      <li>Upgrade options for additional features</li>
      <li>Downgrade options (previous work is saved, but its visibility or use may be limited)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-tip">
      <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Annual plans typically offer significant savings compared to monthly billing. Check your plan options for available discounts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-info">
      <h3>Understanding Plan Changes</h3>
      <p><strong>When you upgrade:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access to new features is immediate</li>
        <li>Create more banners based on your new plan limits</li>
        <li>Get access to advanced and exclusive features and priority support</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>When you downgrade:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Existing work is preserved but may not be visible</li>
        <li>Advanced features may become unavailable</li>
        <li>You can re-upgrade at any time to restore full functionality</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Settings Section</h2>
    <p>Configure app general preferences</p>

    <h3>Interface Language</h3>
    <p>Available in multiple languages</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Choose your preferred language for the app interface</li>
      <li>Changes apply immediately</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Email Address</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Enter the email address you would like to use for the App's communications.</li>
      <li>Receive notifications about:</li>
      <ul>
        <li>Banner performance</li>
        <li>System updates</li>
        <li>New features</li>
        <li>Important announcements</li>
      </ul>
    </ul>

    <h3>Premium Features Toggle</h3>
    <p>In certain plans, the premium features are shown grayed out and disabled.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Control the visibility of premium features in the app interface</li>
      <li>Show/Hide Premium Features</li>
    </ul>


    <h3>Customer Data Export</h3>
    <p>Generate and email a customer data export report for privacy compliance. This includes all data stored for a specific customer in our system.</p>

    <h4>Manual Data Export</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Enter a customer email address</li>
      <li>Generate and send them a complete data export report</li>
      <li>Receive the export via email</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-note">
      <p>This generates the same report that is automatically sent when customers request their data through Shopify's GDPR tools. The email will be sent using your configured email templates.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-info">
      <p><strong>Export includes:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>All configured banners and their settings</li>
      <li>Support messages and interactions</li>
      <li>Application interaction logs (last 30 days)</li>
      <li>Any stored preferences or settings</li>
      <li>GDPR compliance information</li>
    </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-note">
      <p><strong>Privacy First:</strong> We respect your privacy and only collect data necessary to improve your experience. You have full control over your data preferences.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-tip">
      <p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Make use of the compliance with data privacy regulations like GDPR. Make sure to have the customer's consent before exporting their data.</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <div class="mt-12 flex gap-4">
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/ai-features`} class="btn bg-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-300">
        ← Previous: AI Features
      </a>
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/support-feedback`} class="btn btn-primary">
        Next: Support & Feedback →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
